# Allowlist: ignore everything, then re-include exactly what docker/Dockerfile COPYs. Anything
# new stays out of the build context by default -- keystores, .env files, release tarballs, and
# the host target/, whose stale cargo fingerprints once made the final build a no-op that shipped
# the dep-cache stub binary.
*

# Root manifests
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock

# The licence, and the third-party notices CI generates (docker.yml); a local build has none
!LICENSE
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt

# The pinned web build the image serves
!apps.lock.json

# Sources the image is built from
!crates
!migrations
!manifests

# ...minus what never belongs in them: build output, secrets, local state.
**/target
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.DS_Store
